  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "chillout: a soft four on the floor with a clap on two and four, a swung offbeat hat and a light shaker, a root-and-fifth bass that walks, and warm electric-piano sevenths once a bar",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "One bar: the kick on every beat a little under full weight, the clap (preferred by its hold over the snare's) on two and four, the loose hat on the ands swung to 0.58, a shaker on the off-sixteenths low in the mix. The bass walks root, fifth, root, third in halves; a stacked-seventh chord on a warm struck keyboard lands on one each bar. Played under the Downtempo tile's spell at 80-90 (round G4).",
